| P2 — playback discards the WAV header | major | P5, P8, P9 | The player receives the **complete WAV** — header and data chunk, every byte the synthesis returned or the clip holds (a player reads the format from the header on its stdin); `played_ms` is derived from accepted **data** bytes only, through the `data_offset` `parse_wav` returns. AC1's "received all 48 044 bytes" and AC3's "accepts exactly 128 000 of the 320 000 data bytes" are both asserted on the runner's byte log. |
