### P2: Executor validates and releases `audio_ref` leases exactly as `image_ref` (R4; AC14)
- **Files:** [`core/actions.py`, `tests/test_observations.py`]
- **Description:** In `ActionExecutor._reject_parts` the lease loop skips only parts whose type is neither `PART_TYPE_IMAGE_REF` nor `PART_TYPE_AUDIO_REF`: an `audio_ref` must resolve in the store with `ref.run_id == call.run_id`, be unexpired on the executor clock and carry `size == ref.size`, else `ERROR_INVALID_RESULT` with the same message forms (the provider's result is not adopted). `_discard_images` discards both reference types (name kept; docstring "every attachment reference"). The observation-size rule already goes through `observation_size` (P1). No other executor logic changes in this step (R10 is P3).
